⍙_R←⍙_PATH APL2TXT ⍙_RA;⍙_CC;⍙_DATA;⍙_E;⍙_EXT;⍙_FILE;⍙_L;⍙_NAME;⍙_NC;⍙_OBJ;⍙_OW;⍙_T;⍙_TIE;⍙_TIME;⍙_TXT;⍙_U;⍙_V;⎕IO
⍝ Create a unicode txt file in the supplied directory (⍙_PATH) showing the
⍝ contents of the given function or variable (where 1⊃⍙_RA=⍙_OBJ) is a cvec
⍝ name of an object in the current workspace) in a unicode based text file
⍝ that any text editor can understand without APL+Win.

⍝ If ⍙_PATH is '', the file is created in the same path as the current ws.

⍝ ⍙_OW (2⊃⍙_RA) is a bit indicating behavior if the destination text
⍝ file exists already (1=overwrite).

⍝ ⍙_CC (3⊃⍙_RA) is a bit indicating whether or not the resulting file
⍝ should be case coded or not.  Case codes work like this (from Dyalog's
⍝ ]LINK.CaseCode documentation):
⍝
⍝   HelloWorld    - has the uppercase indication
⍝   1000010000    - which when reversed is
⍝   0000100001    - which is binary for
⍝   33 Base 10    - which in octal is
⍝   41 Base 8     - so the full name including case code is:
⍝   HelloWorld-41

⍝   No case code (default): <HelloWorld> -> HelloWorld.txt

⍝   With case code: <HelloWorld> -> HelloWorld-41.txt

⍝ The result is a character vector message indicating success or failure.

⍝                ↓⍙_PATH            ↓⍙_OBJ   ↓⍙_OW ↓⍙_CC
⍝ Used like: MSG←'C:\temp\' APL2TXT 'CMIOTA' 0     0

⍝ Some key APL symbols and their Unicode code points in decimal:

⍝ AV
⍝ Ind Symbol-Unicode dec.      Unicode hex.
⍝ --- -----------------------  ------------
⍝ 1   ⎕TCNUL (Null) - 0        (U+0000)
⍝ 2   ⍀ - (Undefined) - 0      (U+0000)
⍝ 3   € (Euro) - 8364          (U+20AC)
⍝ 4   ⍷ (Epsilon-Underscore) - 9079 (U+2377)
⍝ 5   ⋄ (Diamond) - 9671       (U+25C7)
⍝ 6   ¨ (Diaeresis) - 168      (U+00A8)
⍝ 7   ← (Left Arrow) - 8592    (U+2190)
