⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,69 70 71 72 73 74 75 76 77 78 79 80 81 82 83 84 85 86 87 88 89 90
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,91 92 93 94 95 96 97 98 99 100 101 102 103 104 105 106 107 108 109
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,110 111 112 113 114 115 116 117 118 119 120 121 122 123 124 125 126
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,8802 199 252 233 226 228 224 8800 231 234 235 232 239 238 8968 196
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,8970 201 8710 215 244 246 9109 251 9054 9017 214 220 162 163 165
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,9066 9064 225 237 243 250 241 209 9053 9024 191 9015 245 248 253
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,161 171 187 9109 9109 9109 124 124 124 124 43 43 124 124
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,43 43 43 43 43 192 193 194 195 196 197 198 199 200 201
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,202 203 204 205 206 207 45 209 210 211 212 213 214 43 216 217
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,218 219 220 221 124 255 9082 223 9075 9060 227 9073 8869 8868
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,9021 8854 9074 9023 8711 9033 8712 8745 8801 9049 8805 8804 9045
⍝ ⍙_T←⍙_T,9038 247 34 8728 9675 8744 9076 8746 175 8739 255

⍝ Convert mat to ⎕TCLF delimited (UNIX style) vector:
⍝ If v19 is in use, use ⎕CV (for speed) else, use DTBV logic:
:If 19≤⎕FI 2↑⎕SYSVER ⋄ ⍙_DATA←⎕TCLF ⎕CV ⍙_DATA
:Else ⋄ ⍙_U←+/∨\' '≠⌽⍙_DATA ⋄ ⍙_DATA←⍙_U↑¨⊂[⎕IO+1]⍙_DATA
   ⍙_DATA←⎕ENLIST ⍙_DATA,¨⎕TCLF
:EndIf
⍝ Convert from ⎕AV internal UCS structure to UTF-8 (unicode):
 ⍙_TXT←'X-AV-UCS' 'UTF-8' ⎕UCS ⍙_DATA ⍝ Now we have unicode chars

⍝ Add a case code? This is for workspace's with functions whose names
⍝ only differ by case (e.g. Foo vs foo) as Windows does not allow for
⍝ filenames that differ only in case:
:If ⍙_CC ⋄ ⍙_T←⎕ENLIST ⍕¨⌽⍙_OBJ∊⎕AV[65+⍳26] ⍝ Bits of upper chars, reversed
  ⍝ e.g. Foo -> Foo-1, foo -> foo-0)
   ⍙_CC←'-',2 8 ⍙EZBase ⍙_T ⍝ 2: Binary, 8: Octal
:Else ⋄ ⍙_CC←'' ⍝ No case code
:EndIf

⍝ Using .txt makes most text editors see the file as UTF-8!
 ⍙_NAME←⍙_OBJ,⍙_CC,⍙_EXT
 ⍙_FILE←⍙_PATH,⍙_NAME
 ⍙_TIE←⎕NNUMS,⎕XNNUMS ⋄ ⍙_TIE←-((⍳⍴⍙_TIE)∊∣⍙_TIE)⍳0

⍝ Does the file already exist?:
:If 1∊(⍙_NAME,' ')⍷(⎕LIB ⍙_PATH),' '
  :If ⍙_OW ⍝ Overwrite exising file?
     ⍙_FILE ⎕XNTIE ⍙_TIE
     ⍙_FILE ⎕XNERASE ⍙_TIE
  :Else ⋄ ⍙_R←'File not created. "',⍙_FILE,'" already exists.' ⋄ →0
  :EndIf
:EndIf

⍝ Create output file, write to it, untie it:
 ⍙_FILE ⎕XNCREATE ⍙_TIE
 ⍙_TXT ⎕NAPPEND ⍙_TIE
 ⎕NUNTIE ⍙_TIE
⍝ Set the file's timestamp to the APL+Win timestamp of the source object.
⍝ Insert dummy day of week value in position 3 so we get an 8 elm vec we
⍝ can convert to windows file time structure:
 ⍙_TIME←2 ⎕AT ⍙_OBJ ⋄ ⍙_TIME←(2↑⍙_TIME),0,2↓⍙_TIME
⍝ Convert 8-elm vec to 2 32bit ints for filetime:
 ⍙_TIME←2⊃⎕WCALL 'SystemTimeToFileTime' ⍙_TIME (2⍴0)
 ⍙_T←'FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES' 'FILE_SHARE_READ FILE_SHARE_WRITE' 0 'OPEN_EXISTING' 0 0
 ⍙_U←⎕WCALL 'CreateFile' ⍙_FILE,⍙_T
 ⍙_V←⎕WCALL 'SetFileTime' ⍙_U 0 0 ⍙_TIME ⋄ ⍙_V←⎕WCALL 'CloseHandle' ⍙_U
 ⍙_R←'"',⍙_FILE,'" created.' ⍝ Success
